tests[1]:
  - command: npm run coverage
    path: test/lineage.test.ts
    scope: project
    assert_stdout_contains[1]: thresholds met
    note: a padded environment identity cannot slip past the contamination refusal
close_reason: "asString now returns the trimmed value, so every identity read through it - environment ids, evaluation contexts, seed sets - is normalized at parse time before any strict-equality comparison. Docstring records why this is a correctness requirement rather than a convenience.\n\nVerified with an ADVERSARIAL test rather than a mutation test: it builds a spec declaring environment_version as two spaces, env-eval, tab, parses it through parseGenerationSpec so normalization happens on the real code path rather than in a hand-built literal, then asserts findContaminationPath still catches it against the held-out id env-eval. Reverting asString to return the raw value turns that test red, 23 of 24 passing; with the fix, 24 of 24.\n\nrelease:check green, coverage still an exact 100/100/100 across 9 files."
body: ""
